{"step_index":9750,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T09:03:55Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Antigravity (AGY) & Gemini Hard Enforcement Suite\\nAuthor: Antigravity AI (Pair Programming with Iraq Bhai)\\nTarget: Any Antigravity / Gemini CLI Native Linux VM Environment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview of the Enforcement Files\\n\\nThese files are the exact core configuration and policy files that force Google Antigravity (AGY) and Gemini CLI to strictly obey all rules, restrictions, and safety directives.\\n\\n| File Name | Original VM Path | Role & How It Forces Compliance |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `hooks.json` | `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json` | **Physical Runtime Interceptor.** Configured as a `PreToolUse` hook. Before any tool (`run_command`, `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`) is executed by the agent, Antigravity physically pauses execution and passes the payload to `delete_guard.py`. If the hook returns `deny`, execution is physically stopped at the OS level. |\\n| `delete_guard.py` | `~/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/delete_guard.py` | **The Rule Evaluator Script.** Contains regex and AST inspections for 27+ destructive rules: intercepts `rm`, `unlink`, `rmdir`, `sudo`, `truncate`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean`, `shred`, `dd`, `rsync --delete`, python deletion, file overwrites of protected files. Returns JSON `decision: allow` or `decision: deny`. |\\n| `GEMINI.md` | `~/GEMINI.md` | **Root User Directives & Global Rules.** Loaded by Antigravity CLI on startup as `<RULE[/home/azureuser/GEMINI.md]>`. The model is prompted with highest system priority. Enforces Bengali response language, addressing as 'ইরাক ভাইয়া', single asterisks, absolute file paths, and the Master Architecture. |\\n| `AGENTS.md` | `~/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md` | **Canonical Hierarchical Agent Architecture.** Defines supervisor topology (`agy:0`, `agy:ask`, `agy:report`, `agy:action`), Safety Levels (0, 1, 2A, 2B, 3), and approval gating. |\\n| `safety_levels.json`| `~/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/safety_levels.json` | **Machine-Readable Safety Matrix.** Defines operations permitted under Safety Levels 0, 1, 2A, 2B, 3. |\\n| `protected_regist\n<truncated 1498 bytes>","Description":"\"Create README guide for the enforcement suite\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/exports/AGY_RULES_AND_HOOKS/README_ENFORCEMENT_GUIDE.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing enforcement guide\"","toolSummary":"\"Create enforcement guide\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
